        "date": "2026-10-12",
        "author": "Boris Delange",
        "message": "Add the RxNorm ingredient argipressin (19006871) with its descendants. Argipressin is the INN of arginine vasopressin, the vasopressin used in intensive care, and RxNorm carries it as a standard Ingredient separate from vasopressin (USP) (1507835). Its descendants, which include the European products Empressin and Reverpleg, were not reached by the vasopressin (USP) anchor, so a site mapping its vasopressin to them was counted as not covered."
      }
